## Authentication & Authorization

- [ ] **Implement AWS Cognito authentication for shared ALB**
  - Create AWS Cognito User Pool and User Pool Client
  - Configure User Pool Domain for hosted UI
  - Create Cognito User Pool groups: `argocd-admin`, `argocd-platform`, `argocd-devops`, `argocd-auditor`
  - Configure ALB listener rules with Cognito authentication for protected paths:
    - **Public paths (no auth required):**
      - `/` - Landing page
      - `/healthz` - ArgoCD health check (ALB health check endpoint)
      - `/argocd/healthz` - ArgoCD health check (with path prefix)
      - `/atlantis/healthz` - Atlantis health check
      - `/reader/api/v1/health` - Bitwarden Reader health check
    - **Protected paths (require authentication):**
      - `/argocd/*` - Require authentication (except health check paths above)
      - `/atlantis/*` - Require authentication (except health check paths above)
      - `/reader/*` - Require authentication (except health check paths above)
  - **Important:** Configure listener rule priorities so health check paths are matched before protected paths (higher priority = evaluated first)
  - Ensure OAuth/OIDC callback URLs are configured correctly
  - Enable SSO across apps via shared session cookies

- [ ] **Configure ArgoCD RBAC with Cognito OIDC integration**
  - Configure OIDC in ArgoCD (`argocd-cm` ConfigMap) to use Cognito as identity provider
  - Set up RBAC policies in `argocd-rbac-cm` ConfigMap with custom roles:
    - `role:admin` - Full access (map to `argocd-admin` Cognito group)
    - `role:platform` - Manage clusters, repos, projects (map to `argocd-platform` Cognito group)
    - `role:devops` - Manage applications in specific projects (map to `argocd-devops` Cognito group)
    - `role:readonly` - Read-only access (map to `argocd-auditor` Cognito group)
  - Configure project-scoped permissions for DevOps role
  - Set default policy to `role:readonly` for conservative access
  - Ensure Cognito groups are included in OIDC token claims
